  "notes": [
   "Step 1 parts were correct; no parts added or removed.",
   "Breadboard hole naming follows the catalogue: bank 'b' = rows f-j (the half where the image shows the LEDs, drawn at the top), bank 't' = rows a-e (the half where the blue wires land). Resistors straddle the centre gap, leg 1 in row f and leg 2 in row e of the same column number.",
   "Pins: Uno 6 -> LED1, 5 -> LED2, 4 -> LED3, 3 -> LED4, 2 -> LED5, each through a 220 ohm resistor on the anode side, as in the schematic.",
   "LED anode is the leg in the same column as the resistor (straight leg); the cathode is the neighbouring column, wired by a short black wire to the top ground rail (tn). The rail is wired to Uno GND.1.",
   "Rail hole numbers on tn are approximate (the rail is one strip, so any hole is equivalent)."
  ]
 },
